quran[7]{c,v,t}:
  6,125,"Whoever Allah intends to guide, He expands his breast for Islam. But whoever He intends to leave astray, He makes his breast narrow and tight, as if he were climbing up into the sky. Thus, Allah lays (spiritual) defilement on those who do not believe."
  6,126,This is your Lord’s path—perfectly straight. We have clearly explained the revelations for a people mindful (of advice).
  6,127,"For them shall be the Abode of Peace with their Lord, and He shall be their Guardian because of what they have been doing."
  6,128,"On the Day when He would assemble them all together, (He shall say:) ‘O company of jinn! You have misled many of the humans.’ Their friends from among the humans will say: ‘Our Lord! We benefited from one another, and (now) we have reached our term which You had appointed for us.’ He will say: ‘The Fire is your abode, to remain in it forever, except what Allah may wish. Indeed, your Lord is All-Wise, All-Knowing.’"
  6,129,That is how We make the wrongdoers allies of one another because of what they used to earn.
  6,130,"(Allah will ask:) ‘O company of jinn and humans! Did messengers not come to you from yourselves, proclaiming My revelations to you and warning you of the meeting of this Day of yours?’ They will say: ‘We testify against ourselves.’ The life of this world had deceived them, and they would bear witness against themselves that they had been disbelievers."
  6,131,This (sending of messengers) is because your Lord would never destroy towns unjustly while their people were unaware (of the truth).
